# FunCrash GAMEPLAY (Baccarat) bot: the casino/hedge commands
# (/testbaccarat, /pair, /pairs, /delpair, /run, /stoprun, /runs, /runlog)
# driving Evolution Baccarat A on funcrash.com -- acc1 always bets BANKER,
# acc2 always bets PLAYER on the SAME hand at the SAME table, so the money
# mostly moves between the two accounts and only the ~5% banker commission
# bleeds. Same flow and the same engine as .env.gameplay (cricmatch) and
# .env.winclash.gameplay; only the site profile differs. No signup commands
# here -- funcrash's signup markup has never been inspected.
#
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-10-21 with verify_baccarat.py (read-only, no bets),
# from a laptop with no proxy, on both client-supplied ids:
#   * login completes and the AWS WAF clears on its own (the soft
#     "challenge" action) -- no CapSolver spend was needed on either run,
#     though a key is still required in case it escalates to "captcha".
#   * the launch route works: /casinoRedirect?q=86&provider=evolution lands
#     on ezugi.evo-games.com -- the same Evolution client this engine drives
#     everywhere else. Seat to live table took 35s and 32s.
#   * BOTH IDS OPEN THE SAME PHYSICAL TABLE, id nx7ecktjzywdqwwt (which is
#     also the table cricmatch's and winclash's Baccarat A reach). That is
#     the precondition for a hedge -- a run aborts before any bet if the two
#     sides land on different tables.
#   * chip rail 100 / 500 / 2500 / 10000 / 50000 / 100000, so the TABLE
#     MINIMUM IS 100 RUPEES A SIDE. The in-game footer agrees:
#     "Baccarat A Rs 100-500,000". A /run below 100 is refused.
#   * both bet spots present (bet-spot-Banker, bet-spot-Player), balances
#     readable, 2 clean betting windows in 60s on a ~35s cycle.
#
# NOT verified yet: no bet has ever been placed on funcrash. Do one
#     /run <pair> 100 1
# and read /runlog before scaling the amount or the number of rounds.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-funcrash-gameplay-bot-token-from-botfather
# One id, or several comma-/space-separated ids for multiple master admins:
# MASTER_ADMIN_ID=111111111,222222222
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=your-telegram-user-id

# REQUIRED on funcrash, same as winclash and unlike cricmatch/khelofun.
# Every page load here can be met by an AWS WAF interstitial (confirmed on
# the wire: 202 + x-amzn-waf-action: challenge from server awselb/2.0). The
# soft "challenge" clears itself for free, which is what both verified runs
# got; the hard "captcha" needs a solved token. Without a key a run that
# lands on the hard action fails with a clear message rather than hanging.
CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=your-capsolver-api-key

BOT_MODE=gameplay
BOT_SITE_URL=https://funcrash.com/
ADMINS_FILE=admins.funcrash.gameplay.json
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.funcrash.gameplay.json
ADMIN_PHONES_FILE=admin_phones.funcrash.gameplay.json
# Pair credentials + run history. MUST be distinct from every other
# instance's files -- each process reads them once at import and rewrites
# them whole on every save, so two bots sharing a path silently clobber
# each other. (pairs.* holds plaintext passwords; both patterns are
# gitignored.)
PAIRS_FILE=pairs.funcrash.gameplay.json
PAIR_RUNS_FILE=pair_runs.funcrash.gameplay.json

# How many /run hedge sessions may execute at once. Default 3; set to 6 for
# the client's "5-6 runs at a time".
#
# Read the cost before raising it further. EACH RUN DRIVES TWO CHROMIUMS
# holding a live video table, so 6 runs = 12 browsers on one box. That is
# the same seat budget TOURNAMENT_MAX_SEATS defaults to (12) for the
# 32-core VPS, and the 2026-08-23 starexch run shows what overshooting
# looks like: 30 live-video Chromiums finished nothing in 94 minutes while
# a 3-seat group on the same code played clean hands immediately. The
# machine is the ceiling, not the site.
#
# Two more limits that bite before this number does:
#   * 6 runs need 12 DISTINCT accounts. run_cmd refuses a pair that shares
#     any username with a running pair -- betting one login from two
#     contexts corrupts both hedges.
#   * every run goes out through the ONE global proxy (/setproxy), so 6
#     runs means 12 logins from a single exit IP in a couple of minutes,
#     into a site whose WAF blocks per IP and behaviourally. More proxy
#     IPs is the real fix; there is no tuning around it.
MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=6
